  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Top up COPOLAD III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This TOP UP is part of the Multi-Annual Regional Indicative Programme for Latin America and the Caribbean for the financial period 2021&#xbf;2027. Its objectives include strengthening regional cooperation platforms and promoting the adoption of preventive and comprehensive approaches to drug policy. It aims to ensure effective coordination of national, regional, and bi-regional responses to justice and security issues, while integrating health, economic, social, and environmental dimensions. The focus is on prevention, the reduction of violence, and the disruption of the economic and social structures that sustain drug trafficking, particularly in the most affected areas and trafficking corridors. Furthermore, the amendment supports the implementation of the priorities jointly agreed upon by the European Union and Latin American and Caribbean countries in the 2024 La Paz Declaration, and will continue to do so throughout its five-year duration&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
